codex
Most requested machinery is present and exercised by contract tests. One implementation discrepancy is emerging in the reporting path: the D2 complementarity JSON is labeled as having “no row-level intervals,” but the generic function still writes Wilson `lo`/`hi` objects. I’m checking the binding spec and the remaining guards before assigning severity and deciding whether it gates the full run.
exec
/bin/zsh -lc "nl -ba generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md | sed -n '260,560p'" in /Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd
 succeeded in 0ms:
   260	  estimate of the stitched solution's effective cadence (the stitched bias is
   261	  S_20/S_mix, ~1.1–1.4 under plausible fit weightings, not the ~1.9 endpoint
   262	  contrast at 200 s), is compared with nominal on the same 33-target K=1
   263	  subset using common bootstrap draws, never enters nominal P4 or is pooled
   264	  with nominal surfaces, retains the scenario-invariant published-amplitude
   265	  coordinate, has its own immutable scenario code and final campaign-id
   266	  digit, and adds exactly 33 shards. Dominance is scenario-local; dropout
   267	  stays a nominal-cadence scenario (no dropout × cadence_alt crossing).
   268	- Amendment 4 (post-pilot D2 window stratification, recovery estimand and
   269	  metric corrections; G4 stats + methods both PROCEED-WITH-AMENDMENT-4,
   270	  2026-08-30): the gen1 stratified pilot (144 shards, non-confirmatory,
   271	  archived under generalization/results/2026-08-30_d2_pilot/, entering no
   272	  estimate) exposed two design defects before any confirmatory-era run.
   273	  (1) Window strata: K = 0/1/2 are re-defined on W_g as above; gen1 is
   274	  superseded by gen2 (regenerated atomically with the amended builder).
   275	  (2) Primary P4 = recovery (above); detection-only is secondary.
   276	  (3) Paired controls are scored against their partner's injected truth
   277	  (detection D and strict recovery R; 2×2 tables, B-only/C-only/union,
   278	  target-standardized paired differences with common draws, P(R_B=1,
   279	  R_C=0), quiet-control-conditioned secondary estimand, reuse table); the
   280	  primary denominator is never conditioned on control status and no
   281	  aggregate native-rate subtraction is applied. (4) Metric corrections:
   282	  D2 surfaces at target level on (W_g, published amplitude) with frozen
   283	  edges {15, 41, 84, 217}; chance-match calibration by 10,000 target-level
   284	  derangements with endpoint-aligned numerators; paired contrasts with zero
   285	  observed discordance report the CP discordance bound; D2 row-level
   286	  intervals suppressed (descriptive); `prespecified_primary` /
   287	  `confirmatory_decision` replace the ambiguous `confirmatory` flag (P5
   288	  remains the sole confirmatory decision). (5) Provenance: raw result
   289	  JSONs and sidecars are archived with every pilot record; subset runs are
   290	  bound by `stars_file_sha256` and exact id-set equality; run manifests
   291	  record argv, timestamps and git commit/dirty state. Amendment 4 is
   292	  disclosed as pilot-informed and is not represented as part of the
   293	  original v3 preregistration; no further estimand-hierarchy change is
   294	  permitted after it.
   295	- Generation discipline (Amendment 2, G3 methods findings 1–8): every
   296	  manifest row of every arm carries the fixed typed schema
   297	  (d2_truth_model.MANIFEST_COLUMNS) including an explicit immutable
   298	  `scenario` code and `n_strata_scheduled` (3 nominal, 1 single-window
   299	  sensitivity); shards are built into a staging directory under an
   300	  IN_PROGRESS sentinel from the ATTESTED per-star exposure shards (original
   301	  text tokens preserved; model evaluated on the frozen loader's parse; each
   302	  written shard re-loaded through the frozen loader and checked bitwise on
   303	  epochs), validated (index == manifest == disk, SHA identity, A/B ↔
   304	  injected-mode bijection, exactly K = {0,1,2} nominal-B replicates per
   305	  scheduled target, exact null serials), described by a generation manifest
   306	  (generation id over every input SHA + code SHAs + arguments; per-shard
   307	  SHAs; roster-report and SPOC-report SHAs) and published atomically —
   308	  there is no resume. The runner refuses unpublished generations, binds
   309	  each result's sidecar to shard SHA, result SHA, pass set, env, frozen and
   310	  campaign digests, attestation SHA and generation id, and writes a per-id
   311	  completion table; metrics verify all of it before counting a result.
   312	  Timing pilot = the builder's stratified `pilot_shard_index.txt` (~150
   313	  shards spanning every arm/scenario, window strata and amplitudes) run via
   314	  `--stars-file`; pilot outputs are never confirmatory for P4/P5.
   315	- Truth-model corrections found at implementation (2026-08-28): |sinc| ≥ 0.3
   316	  rejection corresponds to P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence (the earlier "197 s"
   317	  was the |sinc| = 0.5 point); D2 min published period is 115.9 s and 49/103
   318	  stars carry 20-s solutions, so few modes are affected. Phase protocol is
   319	  frozen above (per-mode independent; PCG64(TIC) base; PCG64(TIC·10+d)
   320	  for the two phase-draw variants). Blackbody derivative at 11,500 K gives
   321	  (1.43, 0.80) ≈ the 1.4/0.80 low rung; upper rungs cover
   322	  atmosphere-model/limb-darkening uncertainty; 1.7 is the adopted midpoint.
   323	
   324	## Metrics — see METRICS_SPEC.md (frozen before any campaign L-S run)
   325	
   326	## Execution topology
   327	
   328	- Mac: rosters, fetches, shard building, metrics, figures, git (authoritative).
   329	- Laptop `jacks-7i-5090` (22 workers): replay gate + D3 run. Desktop
   330	  (needs wake; offline 64 d): D2 + D3 overflow; if unreachable, D2 runs on
   331	  the laptop after D3 (+1 day; slip rule below).
   332	- Windows job launches escape the sshd job object via WMI
   333	  `Win32_Process.Create` (Start-Process children die with the ssh session —
   334	  found the hard way on the first replay launch).
   335	- Wall model (anchor 928 ≈ 11 h at 22 workers; cost scales with baseline):
   336	  D3@3,000 ≈ 1.2–1.9 d; D2 core ≈ 1.5 d; hard stop via 150-star pilot.
   337	  Disk binds, not time: `workers = min(22, floor(free_GB × 0.5 / 0.47))`,
   338	  scratch on local NVMe/RAM disk, never a synced folder.
   339	- Results bundles: `generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/` mirroring the
   340	  existing convention (README, DATA_PROVENANCE, SHA256SUMS, acceptance.json).
   341	
   342	## Review gates (sol@xhigh + ChatGPT Pro standing directive)
