    51	
    52	### Campaign source_id convention
    53	
    54	19-digit numeric strings: `90…` D3 targets, `92…` D2 arm B, `93…` D2 arm A,
    55	`94…` D2 Gaussian nulls, `95…` D2 paired real-window controls, `96…` D2
    56	Romero self-window diagnostic. No collision with Gaia DR3 ids; always valid
    57	for the frozen seed convention. D2 arm layout `AA TTTTTTTTTT K GR PS CD`:
    58	K template index 0–2; G/R ladder indices 1–3 (22 = nominal); P phase draw
    59	0–2; S amplitude-scale code 0 = 1.0, 1 = 0.7, 2 = 1.3, 3 = dominant-mode
    60	dropout (scale 1.0); C crowding code 0 = PDCSAP as published, 1 =
    61	SAP-equivalent re-dilution (Amendment 2); D cadence code 0 = frozen rule,
    62	1 = `cadence_alt` pure-120-s endpoint (Amendment 3).
    63	
    64	### Replay gate (blocks everything)
    65	
    66	`replay_gate.py` re-runs the frozen `analyze_star` through `frozen_api` on 25
    67	published stars (all 7 schema-v2 + 18 stride-sampled schema-v1) and
    68	byte-compares against the committed bundle. Comparison tiers: raw-identical;
    69	identical after CRLF→LF normalization (git stored the bundle normalized);
    70	identical after the documented v1→v2 schema transform — 921/928 published
    71	files were written before commit `fa16d7f` (parent `e917bd1`), which added
    72	sparse-input early-exit branches plus the `available`/`unavailable_reason`
    73	keys and bumped `schema_version` 1→2. For any star that yields candidates,
    74	the numeric path is unchanged (the new branches fire only on sparse inputs
    75	that previously crashed; all 7 v2 records exercise exactly those branches).
    76	The downgrade transform removes only the two added keys and byte-compares
    77	everything retained. Gate passes only with a nonempty roster, zero
    78	mismatches AND at least one schema-v2 star reproducing with no transform
    79	(unconditional). VERDICT 2026-08-28 (jacks-7i-5090, production venv):
    80	PASS — 7 identical_newline + 18 identical_v1_schema, 25/25.
    81	Campaign L-S runs are valid only on machine+env pairs that passed the gate;
    82	`run_generalization_ls.py` refuses to start without a matching PASS
    83	attestation (full env fingerprint + frozen SHAs + gate identity). Full
    84	928-star baseline replay running on the production machine (launched
    85	2026-08-28). Panel-stage golden gate (`panel_golden_gate.py`): PASS on both
    86	machines 2026-08-28 — science columns byte-identical vs the published
    87	exposure panel; bjd_tdb ≤ 1 ulp (~40 µs) on ~2.5% of rows (the barycentric
    88	chain sits at rounding boundaries; ns-level IERS-state drift since build
    89	time flips the last bit — measured on the production machine itself);
    90	campaign builds pin IERS via astropy-iers-data with auto_download off.
    91	
    92	### Environment
    93	
    94	The published run's venv (laptop `jacks-7i-5090`) is recorded in
    95	`generalization/env/FROZEN_ENV.md`; the numerics-bearing subset is pinned in
    96	`requirements-frozen.txt` (Python 3.12.12, numpy 2.3.x, scipy 1.16.3, astropy
    97	8.0.1, iers-data 0.2026.7.27, pyerfa 2.0.1.5, pandas 2.3.3). Discrepancy on
    98	record: pip metadata said numpy 2.3.3 but the venv imports 2.3.5; the replay
    99	gate PASSED under 2.3.5 (2026-08-28), making 2.3.5 the pinned authority.
   100	Every campaign-run manifest records `env_versions()` (incl. BLAS vendor and
   101	thread env vars) at runtime.
   102	
   103	## D1 — ZTF white dwarfs (anchor, done)
   104	
   105	The published 2026-08-01 bundle: 19-star truth roster + 928-star catalog.
   106	No re-run; campaign metrics re-read the published per-star JSONs.
   107	
   108	## D3 — ZTF × Kepler delta Scuti (real ZTF light curves, external labels)
   109	
   110	- Labels: Murphy+2019 (VizieR J/MNRAS/485/2380/table1, 14,330 Kepler A/F
   111	  stars; `dSct` flag 0/1/2 — ships its own labeled negative class).
   112	- Amplitude axis: Mo+2026 (J/A+A/710/A245): table2 = 259,883 extracted
   113	  frequencies (SNR>8) for 1,838 delta Scutis → per-star dominant amplitude
   114	  (ppt × 1.0857 → mmag); table1 = confirmed super-Nyquist modes → the
   115	  sub-hour stratum (any confirmed SNF ⇒ real mode above Kepler LC Nyquist
   116	  283.2 µHz ⇒ P < 59 min). This replaces the originally scouted Bowman+2016
   117	  join: Bowman's VizieR table carries no amplitudes; Mo+2026 supersedes it
   118	  (and is itself the published Murphy×Bowman merge, 1,838 stars).
   119	- Roster (`build_d3_roster.py`, rebuilt 2026-08-28 post-G1): gmag ≥ 13.2
   120	  (Murphy/KIC g magnitude — the named saturation proxy), ALL 610 dSct=1
   121	  survivors + ALL 76 dSct=2 (own class, excluded from headline numbers) +
   122	  2,314 dSct=0 negatives as a frozen-seed (20260828) simple random sample
   123	  (inclusion probability exactly 2314/7292, weight exactly 7292/2314;
   124	  sampling_weight column carried into every weighted estimate) = 3,000.
   125	  Before any campaign L-S run, the realized crossmatch mapping and an
   126	  ambiguity-adjudication file are committed (crossmatch frozen as DATA,
   127	  not just procedure). Amplitude coverage of positives:
   128	  456/610 with dominant amplitude; 48 > 10 mmag; 254 in 1–10; 154 < 1;
   129	  290 sub-hour; median 1.77 mmag. The 1–10 mmag log ladder and the
   130	  sub-threshold majority make the completeness turn-on curve the headline
   131	  D3 deliverable, not a defect (pre-registered: risk 2).
   132	  Sub-hour stratum caveat (binding): a confirmed Mo super-Nyquist frequency
   133	  establishes a sub-hour signal in the KEPLER APERTURE, not automatically
   134	  in the ZTF-matched source (blends), and the per-star dominant amplitude
   135	  need not describe the super-Nyquist mode; sub-hour-stratum detections are
   136	  adjudicated in W4 alongside triggered negatives, and Mo amplitude
   137	  sinc-correction status gets verified against the paper in W3.
   138	- Acquisition: frozen `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py --roster roster_d3.csv`
