   140	  `build_panels_generic.py` (nearest-cluster crossmatch, catflags/chi cuts,
   141	  ≥20 exp/band, BJD_TDB at Palomar — all frozen functions).
   142	- Prespecified subsets: crowding (sep < 1.0″, ≤3 objects in cone),
   143	  near-saturation (g ≤ 14.0 flagged; g > 14.0 safe subset — the PRINCIPAL
   144	  robustness lens: KIC g is only a saturation proxy and bright A/F stars
   145	  can still saturate in r; per-epoch saturation is additionally handled by
   146	  the frozen catflags QC).
   147	- Caveat on record: dSct=0 means "not a delta Scuti", not "constant" — the
   148	  D3 negative-class result is a TRIGGER RATE (never called FPR); triggered
   149	  negatives get adjudicated in W4 (plausible real variable vs unexplained).
